.TH SPEEKIFY 1 "July 30, 2026" "Speekify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
speekify \- convert inline text, stdin, a local text/PDF file, or readable URL content into a local WAV file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B speekify
[
.I OPTIONS
]
[
.I SOURCE ...
]
.PP
.B speekify
.B batch
[
.I OPTIONS
]
.I SOURCE ...
.PP
.B speekify
.B setup
[
.I OPTIONS
]
.PP
.B speekify
.B inspect
[
.I OPTIONS
]
[
.I SOURCE ...
]
.PP
.B speekify mcp
[
.I OPTIONS
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Speekify is a Python CLI that turns inline text, piped stdin, a local text/PDF file, or the readable body of a URL into a local WAV file generated with Supertonic v3.
.PP
Generation is synchronously orchestrated by a local Temporal service and worker started automatically by Speekify. The terminal shows progress and then the final WAV path; no Temporal administration is required.
.PP
The service is headless, bound only to 127.0.0.1:7233, and uses a local SQLite database. It remains active while a generation, batch, or Temporal workflow is running. It stops after five minutes with no client and no active workflow; a later generation restarts it with the same on-disk state.
.PP
Homebrew manages Temporal as a formula dependency. With pip, pipx, or uv,
Speekify downloads a pinned official Temporal CLI on first generation, verifies
its published SHA-256, stores it in the user data directory, and reuses it
offline. Automatic provisioning supports macOS and Linux on arm64 and amd64;
Windows is not supported. No separate installation is required.
.PP
The default workflow accepts plain text, piped text, a single URL, or a path to a local
.B .txt , .md , .text ,
or
.B .pdf
file. URL input is reduced to readable article content before synthesis. A file source is read automatically (PDF text is extracted with pypdf) and its name becomes the default output title. By default the source language is auto-detected and synthesized as-is with no translation; English input is translated to French before text to speech only when French synthesis is requested with
.B --lang fr .
Sparse speech tags can be added before generation.
.PP
When passing a URL that contains shell-special characters such as
.B ?
or
.B &
\&(common with YouTube URLs), wrap it in quotes. In shells such as
.BR zsh ,
the shell can reject the command before
.B speekify
starts.
.PP
Use
.B speekify batch
to generate one WAV per file, URL, text item, or supported document found recursively in a directory. Directories are stable-sorted and deduplicated; symlinks are not followed. A batch accepts at most 1,000 unique items and files up to 50 MiB.
.PP
Use
.B speekify setup
to pre-download and warm the local AI models.
Use
.B speekify --doctor
to verify the runtime dependencies, confirm that the AI models load correctly, and get a remediation hint when setup is required. Doctor reports Temporal availability or provisionability but does not download Temporal.
.PP
Use
.B speekify inspect
or
.B speekify --dry-run
to preview extraction, translation, speech tags, and planned output paths without running synthesis.
.PP
Use
.B speekify mcp
to expose Speekify as a local Model Context Protocol server for AI assistants that need to generate WAV files from text, URL content, or summarized news recaps.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I SOURCE
Text to synthesize, a single URL to extract, or a path to a local .txt/.md/.text/.pdf file to read. Omit it only when text is piped on stdin.
.SH MAIN OPTIONS
.TP
.B --url
Force URL extraction mode even if the source looks like plain text.
.TP
.B --title
Override the output file name without the extension.
.TP
.B --voice
Select a Supertonic voice from M1-M5 or F1-F5.
.TP
.B --custom-style-path
Use a Supertonic voice-style JSON file. This overrides
.BR --voice .
.TP
.B --lang
Select the Supertonic ISO 639-1 language code such as en, fr, ja, or na. When omitted, the source language is auto-detected and synthesized without translation;
.B --lang fr
detects English input and translates it to French before synthesis. Other codes synthesize in that language with no translation, and
.B na
is the language-agnostic fallback used when detection fails.
.TP
.B --speed
Adjust the playback speed multiplier.
.TP
.B --steps
Set the synthesis step count.
.TP
.B --max-chunk-length
Set the maximum internal Supertonic chunk length.
.TP
.B --silence-duration
Set the silence inserted between Supertonic chunks.
.TP
.B --english-islands / --no-english-islands
When the language is fr, pronounce known English tech terms as English islands.
.TP
.B --english-lexicon-path
Use a newline-delimited file of extra English terms for French synthesis.
.TP
.B --output-dir
Write the generated WAV file into a specific directory.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Inspect the generation plan without creating audio.
.TP
.B --verbose
Show technical diagnostics such as the log file path.
.TP
.B --version
.TP
.B -v
Print the installed Speekify version and exit.
.TP
.B --doctor
Run installation diagnostics, verify runtime dependencies, attempt to load the AI models, and suggest
.B speekify setup
when repair or download is required.
.TP
.B -h
.TP
.B --help
Show the command help and exit.
.SH SETUP OPTIONS
.TP
.B --skip-translation
Do not warm up the English to French translation model.
.TP
.B --verbose
Show technical diagnostics such as the log file path.
.TP
.B -h
.TP
.B --help
Show setup help and exit.
.SH INSPECT OPTIONS
.TP
.B speekify inspect
Accepts the same source, URL, language, voice, chunking, and output options as the main generation command, but does not synthesize or write a WAV file.
.SH BATCH BEHAVIOR
The
.B speekify batch
command accepts the common title, voice, language, speed, steps, chunking, English-island, output-directory, and verbose options. It does not accept
.BR --url " or " --dry-run .
.PP
Up to four item workflows may be in flight. The preparation worker runs at most two activities concurrently, while one local audio worker serializes synthesis. Successful items are kept when another item fails; the command exits non-zero if any item failed.
.SH MCP SERVER
The
.B speekify mcp
entry point runs an MCP server over stdio by default. It exposes the
.B speekify_generate_wav
tool for converting inline text, readable URL content, or a local .txt/.md/.text/.pdf file into a WAV file,
.B speekify_generate_batch
for multiple files, URLs, text items, or directories,
.B speekify_generation_defaults
for supported voices and language defaults, and a
.B news_recap_to_audio
prompt for source-summary-to-audio automations.
.PP
The generation tool accepts CLI-equivalent controls including English-island handling, custom English lexicon path, and optional user-config defaults.
.TP
.B --transport
Select the MCP transport, either stdio or streamable-http.
.SS Connecting AI clients
Local clients use the default stdio transport; remote clients such as ChatGPT use streamable-http.
.TP
.B Claude Code
Register the local server, then run /mcp inside Claude Code to confirm it:
.PP
.RS
.B claude mcp add --transport stdio speekify -- speekify mcp
.RE
.TP
.B Codex
Register the local server, or add an [mcp_servers.speekify] block to ~/.codex/config.toml:
.PP
.RS
.B codex mcp add speekify -- speekify mcp
.RE
.TP
.B ChatGPT / OpenAI
Start the HTTP transport, which serves http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp, then expose it behind a reachable HTTPS URL (or an OpenAI Secure MCP Tunnel) and register that URL in the client:
.PP
.RS
.B speekify mcp --transport streamable-http
.RE
.PP
See docs/mcp-clients.md for full per-client setup, including GitHub Copilot.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B speekify "Hello world"
Generate a WAV file from inline text.
.TP
.B speekify --lang fr "Hello world"
Generate French speech.
.TP
.B speekify https://example.com/article
Extract readable article text and synthesize it.
.TP
.B speekify "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eSP7PLTXNy8"
Extract a YouTube transcript. Quote URLs that contain shell-special characters such as
.B ?
\&.
.TP
.B printf 'Hello from stdin' | speekify
Read the text from standard input.
.TP
.B speekify --doctor
Check dependencies, model availability, and installation health.
.TP
.B speekify --dry-run https://example.com/article
Preview URL extraction and planned audio paths without synthesis.
.TP
.B speekify inspect "Hello world"
Inspect inline text generation without creating a WAV file.
.TP
.B speekify setup
Download and warm the local AI models.
.TP
.B speekify batch article.pdf https://example.com ./notes
Generate one WAV per source and recursively expand the directory.
.TP
.B speekify mcp
Run the MCP server for local AI clients over stdio.
.TP
.B speekify mcp --transport streamable-http
Run the MCP server with streamable HTTP transport for local experiments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Speekify/runtime/speekify.log
Runtime log file on macOS.
.TP
.I ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/speekify/runtime/speekify.log
Runtime log file on Linux and other supported POSIX installations.
.TP
.I <data directory>/temporal/temporal.db
Persistent local Temporal SQLite database.
.TP
.I <data directory>/jobs, batches, reports
Private generation receipts/prepared sources, batch manifests/results, and redacted reports. Set
.B SPEEKIFY_DATA_DIR
to override the platform data directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/speekify/config.toml
Optional TOML file for generation defaults. Set
.B SPEEKIFY_CONFIG
to use another config path. Explicit CLI options override config values.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command exits with status 0 on success and non-zero on failure. The
.B --doctor
command exits non-zero when dependencies are missing or when one of the models cannot be loaded. A batch exits non-zero if at least one item failed.
.SH NETWORK AND PRIVACY
Inline text, local file contents, Temporal state, and audio synthesis are not sent to a hosted TTS or Temporal service. Network access is used to fetch requested URLs or YouTube transcripts, download AI models, and provision the pinned Temporal CLI for pip/pipx/uv. Temporal telemetry, newsfeed, and inherited OTEL exporters are disabled.
.PP
Remote MCP transports carry tool arguments between the remote client and the Speekify endpoint or tunnel; use stdio when the complete client-to-Speekify path must remain local.
